message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file. Read the section 'Status and known gaps' in the README before citing any number."
type: software
title: "Multi-Agent Smart Water Distribution with Computer Vision-Based Container Detection and AI-Driven Behavior Forecasting for Disaster Relief in Smart Cities: code and simulation"
abstract: >-
  Code for an edge-based multi-agent water dispenser system for disaster relief.
  Each dispenser is an autonomous agent that checks the container with a camera model,
  forecasts short-term demand, chooses between dispensing, waiting and forwarding the
  request to a neighbour with a PPO-trained policy, and communicates over MQTT,
  point-to-point LoRa or NB-IoT without a cloud service. Includes the simulator,
  training scripts, gateway scripts, dashboards and a software-in-the-loop deployment.
  The agent code has been tested against simulated peripherals only; the trained
  detector, the trial hardware logs and the trial broker configuration are not included.
